    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run \u2014 the acceptance suite is the only test module). \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **429** once 100+ owners already exist with today's `registrationDate`.\n\nMirroring the existing `CheckCityCapacity` pattern, I added:\n\n- **`CheckDailyLimit.java`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws `DailyLimitExceededException` when the count reaches `MAX_PER_DAY = 100`.\n- **`DailyLimitExceededException.java`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 checked exception carrying the count.\n- **`DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with `{\"errors\":[\"dailyLimit\"]}`.\n- **`...DailyLimitExceededException.yml`** (`officefloor/escalation/`) \u2014 wires the handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step (under `transaction` governance) after `checkCityCapacity` and before `build`, so the count is taken before the new owner is constructed/saved.\n\nThe check runs before `BuildOwner` (where a new owner's `registrationDate` defaults to today), so the 101st create of the day sees exactly 100 existing owners dated today and is rejected \u2014 matching the acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit`.",
